Subject: [PATCH] feat: draw inline texture and atlas icons in text

FontStrings and GameTooltip lines dropped |T...|t and |A...|a escapes
with the other markup, so text after an icon moved left and measured
widths left the icons out; the client draws the icons in the line and
GetStringWidth includes them.

- sim_render::inline_markup splits text into text pieces and icons:
  path or file ID, height (0 = font height), width (missing or 0 =
  height), offsets, texel rectangle and vertex color of |T; atlas,
  size, offsets and color of |A (with or without the colon after |A).
- Text with an icon is laid out piece by piece: icons become textured
  quads centered on their line, atlases draw their own @crop: region,
  word wrap may move an icon to the next line. Text without icons takes
  the unchanged paths.
- WowFontSystem::measure_markup_width adds the icons' widths; it backs
  GetStringWidth, FontString auto width and GameTooltip width selection.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
