 Without CASC every Blizzard font path maps to one fallback family: the font file `WOW_SIM_FALLBACK_FONT` names, else the first system face. The first system face differs between operating systems, so renders compared across machines pin the fallback.
 
+## Inline icons in text
+
+Text may hold texture escapes, `|Tpath-or-fileID:height:width:offsetX:offsetY:texWidth:texHeight:left:right:top:bottom:r:g:b|t`, and atlas escapes, `|A:atlas:height:width:offsetX:offsetY:r:g:b|a` (Blizzard's `CreateAtlasMarkup` writes the colon after `|A`; without it the escape parses the same). Every field after the path or atlas name is optional. `sim_render::inline_markup` splits a string into text pieces, with colors and hyperlinks stripped as by `strip_wow_markup`, and icons. A height of 0 is the font's height, a missing or zero width is the icon's height, offsets are in UI units with y up, the texel rectangle becomes texture coordinates of `texWidth`×`texHeight`, and the 0–255 color tints the icon.
+
+FontStrings, their color segments and GameTooltip lines that hold an icon are laid out piece by piece (`src/render/glyph/inline_emit.rs`): text pieces are shaped and drawn as before, each icon becomes a textured quad as wide as it is, vertically centered on its line, and word wrap may move an icon to the next line. An atlas draws its own `@crop:` region of the atlas file; a file ID resolves through the interface manifest; an unknown atlas or file ID draws nothing but keeps its room. Text without icons takes the unchanged paths.
+
+`WowFontSystem::measure_markup_width` measures the first line with the icons' widths. `GetStringWidth`, FontString auto-width and GameTooltip width selection use it, so a tooltip line with icons is as wide as its text plus its icons. Wrapped-height measurement still shapes the text without the icons.
+
+Not checked against the client: a size of 0 as the font's height rather than its line height, a zero width of an atlas escape as square rather than the atlas's aspect ratio, and the line keeping its height when an icon is taller than the font.
+
 ## FontString smooth scaling
 
 `0624da720` adds independent `Frame.font_string_smooth_scaling`, shared fractional line-height shaping, mode-keyed caches, and ordinary/runtime/inherited XML handling under retail 12.0.5+. `3c8b48012` adds wrapped render/cache measurement assertions. Contract, inferred-policy boundaries, RED provenance, current GREEN status, earlier XML epoch gap, and future native recorder live in [FontString smooth scaling](../../specs/fontstring-smooth-scaling.md). No native/GPU visual proof is claimed.
